.TH BENCHMARK\-CPU\-PTS 1 "February 2026" "benchmarking" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
benchmark\-cpu\-pts.sh \- benchmark CPU performance using the Phoronix Test Suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B benchmark\-cpu\-pts.sh
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Benchmarks CPU performance using a set of PTS test profiles that together cover
integer, floating-point, cryptographic, compression, and branchy integer workloads.
.PP
The script auto-detects CPU topology (sockets, cores, threads) and scales the
thread count accordingly.
Before running tests it checks the CPU frequency governor, thermal state, system
load, and VM steal time, and warns when conditions may affect result validity.
An unmeasured warmup run is executed before each timed run to bring CPU caches and
branch predictor to steady state.
.PP
PTS is installed automatically on supported distributions (Ubuntu, Debian,
Rocky Linux, openSUSE) if not already present.
.PP
Results are collected into
.B ./benchmark\-results/<result\-id>/
relative to the directory from which the script is invoked.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-threads " " \fIN\fR
Number of threads to use for the benchmark.
Default: all available hardware threads.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-tests " " \fILIST\fR
Comma-separated list of PTS test profile identifiers to run, overriding the
default set.
Default:
.BR pts/build\-linux\-kernel ,
.BR pts/compress\-7zip ,
.BR pts/c\-ray ,
.BR pts/openssl ,
.BR pts/stockfish .
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-runs " " \fIN\fR
Minimum number of timed runs per test.
Default: 3.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-upload
Upload results to OpenBenchmarking.org after the run completes.
Requires \fB\-\-result\-id\fR and \fB\-\-result\-name\fR.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-result\-id " " \fIID\fR
Short identifier for the run (e.g.\&
.IR dc1\-node3\-baseline ).
Used as the output directory name, the PTS result name, and the upload identifier
on OpenBenchmarking.org.
Default: auto-generated timestamp string.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-result\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Human-readable display name for the result (e.g.\&
.IR "DC1 Node3 \- Intel Xeon E5" ).
Required when \fB\-\-upload\fR is specified.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a help message and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
.B ./benchmark\-results/<result\-id>/<result\-id>\-system\-snapshot.txt
System snapshot captured before the run: OS release, kernel version, CPU topology,
frequency scaling state, memory, and processor information from dmidecode.
.TP
.B ./benchmark\-results/<result\-id>/<result\-id>/
PTS result directory containing
.B composite.xml
and all test result data.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run with all available CPU threads:
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./benchmark\-cpu\-pts.sh
.RE
.fi
.PP
Run with a specific thread count:
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./benchmark\-cpu\-pts.sh \-\-threads 4
.RE
.fi
.PP
Run a custom test subset:
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./benchmark\-cpu\-pts.sh \-\-tests pts/compress\-7zip,pts/c\-ray
.RE
.fi
.PP
Run and upload results to OpenBenchmarking.org:
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./benchmark\-cpu\-pts.sh \-\-upload \\
    \-\-result\-id "dc1\-node3\-baseline" \\
    \-\-result\-name "DC1 Node3 \- Intel Xeon E5"
.RE
.fi
